'' -m32 NARROWS A WINDOWS TARGET TO THE FAMILY'S 32-BIT MEMBER, and is refused where
'' the family has none. It must be an error rather than an ignored flag: silently handing
'' a 64-bit binary to someone who asked for 32 is worse than telling them.
''
'' Until 2026-09-04 this test asserted the refusal ON EVERY TARGET -- x86-64 was the only
'' architecture (D14), so there was no 32-bit target left to select. TARGET_WIN32
'' (2026-11-08) brought the family's 32-bit member back, and the refusal now applies to
'' the families that have no such member, which is tests/driver/target-linux64only.test.
'' On a Windows target -m32 selects TARGET_WIN32 -- the MinGW ABI, msvcrt.dll -- and the
'' type layout says so: pointer=32, string descriptor 12.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-types -m32 tests/source/plain.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: target: pointer=32 bits, wchar=2 bytes, string=12 bytes align 4
